From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:23:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] bridge: give the metal backend a shader cache under the
 overlay

The metal backend translates D3D9 shaders through DXVK's front end and
SPIRV-Cross at runtime and keeps the result on disk, keyed by bytecode
hash. dxvk mode already makes cache/dxvk and cache/mesa under the
overlay; metal mode now makes cache/metal and passes its path in
RT_METAL_CACHE_DIR, unless the caller set one, so the backend needs no
new export.
---
 shims/d3d9_bridge.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shims/d3d9_bridge.c b/shims/d3d9_bridge.c
index ddb6009..f6c2c05 100644
--- a/shims/d3d9_bridge.c
+++ b/shims/d3d9_bridge.c
@@ -2541,6 +2541,16 @@ static int metal_init(const char *overlay)
         for (int i = 0; i < 16 && zero; i++) zero = !id[i];
         if (zero) rt_log("gfx deleted %s (null device ID): %s", path, unlink(path) ? "failed" : "ok");
     }
+    /* The backend keeps its translated shaders here, beside the dxvk and
+       mesa caches dxvk mode makes. It is passed in the environment and
+       read when the device is created, so the backend's exports stay
+       the two the bridge already resolves. */
+    snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s/cache", overlay);
+    mkdir(path, 0755);
+    snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s/cache/metal", overlay);
+    mkdir(path, 0755);
+    setenv("RT_METAL_CACHE_DIR", path, 0);
+    rt_log("gfx metal shader cache %s", getenv("RT_METAL_CACHE_DIR"));
     s_lib = dlopen(lib, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
     if (!s_lib) {
         rt_log("gfx missing %s: %s; --gfx null runs without it", lib, dlerror());
